course: dictionary
lesson: 3540
title: The word fee
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fee is an amount of money you pay for a service, or to be allowed to do something. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. Words like pay, price and bank tell you that a fee is about money.
explain: Read this: «When you buy online from another country, the price is changed into your money, and the bank may add a small fee.» The bank adds the fee on top of the price, so a fee is extra money you pay. Ask yourself: what would fit in that gap? Money you pay for something.
explain: Fees come in many kinds. An entrance fee is the money you pay to get into a place, and a late fee is extra money you pay for being late. «Free of charge» means there is no fee at all. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A fee is an amount of money you pay for a service or to be allowed to do something.
fact: «Entrance fee» means money you pay to go into a place, such as a museum or park.
fact: «Late fee» means extra money you pay because you were late with a payment.
fact: «Free of charge» means there is no fee to pay.
fact: Fee is a noun: one fee, and more than one is fees.
exercise: «When you buy online from another country, the bank may add a small fee.» What is the fee in this sentence? | A gift from the bank | A kind of loan to a friend | A page of numbers | *Extra money charged for a service
exercise: «Scammers pretend to be famous YouTubers and footballers giving things away; never send a fee.» What does this sentence tell you to do? | Share your password with them | Ask them for their card code | Send a fee quickly to get the prize | *Never pay money to someone who asks for a fee for free things
exercise: In maths, a park charges an entrance fee of £3 for each child. How much do two children pay? | £5 | *£6 | £2 | £9
test: «Paying a bill late can add a fee on top.» What does add a fee on top mean? | Money taken off your bill | *Extra money charged on top of the bill | A free gift with your bill | A short letter about the bill
test: Which phrase means there is no fee to pay at all? | *Free of charge | Late fee | Entrance fee | School fees
exam: «Scammers pretend to be famous YouTubers giving things away; check their real, official account and never send a fee.» What should you do when an online offer asks for a fee? | Post your card details online | Send your fee at once | Tell them your password | *Check the real, official account and never send a fee
